Each evidence entry is {"quote":"literal substring","start":0,"end":1,"referent":"text referent","attribute":"named attribute or unclear","scope":"one scope value","time":"one time value"}. Each composite binding is {"referent":"compatible referent","attribute":"compatible attribute or unclear","scope":"one scope value","time":"one time value","evidence":[]}; its evidence array uses the same entries. Ambiguous/absent features may have empty evidence. Explicit feature/composite claims need supporting evidence. Scope/time values must come from reference.json. Record multiple bindings separately. The program must validate offsets, schema and evidence consistency; this instruction does not establish its correctness or rater reliability.

Do one first rating per assigned unit. Preserve that first answer and all disagreements. Do not tune definitions, re-rate to improve a match, hide invalid outputs or choose favorable subsets. Any software repair/retry requires a separately retained version and the prospective protocol's declared policy. Human raters are optional. Same-family AI ratings are procedural task separation with shared-model/prior-context limits, not empirical independence or human endorsement.
